      "id": "be-s11-scp-paradigm-c3",
      "heading": "Five forces, technology and barriers to entry",
      "explanation_md": "The **five forces** link to the SCP view of industry profits: **entry**, **power of input suppliers**, **power of buyers**, **industry rivalry**, and **substitutes and complements**. Together they shape the **level, growth and sustainability of industry profits**.\n\n**Technology**: some industries are **labor intensive**, some **capital intensive**, others combine both.\n\n**Barriers to entry**: **capital requirements**, **patents and copyrights**, **economies of scale**, **economies of scope**.\n\nComing next: managing under **perfect competition, monopoly, monopolistic competition and oligopoly**.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Barriers to entry: capital requirements, patents and copyrights, economies of scale, economies of scope.",
      "clarification": null,
